{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":24275,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"36593f13275c320160b3fbf3c4f969b039efdb3ba05e6da2c660b605374c5e29","packTokens":9449,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":143,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"sketches","tokens":9275,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":10,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"sketches"},"pointers":[],"system":"Three engineers independently listed behaviours for the same request. Find where they DISAGREE about what the system should do (not wording differences).\nFor each disagreement: id D-1.., the span, a short topic, and the readings: which sketch (1-3), which behaviour index (0-based) in that span, and a one-line summary. Cite at least two different sketches. Empty list if they agree.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"sketches\" kind=\"sketches\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"sketch\": 1,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Implement all 13 operations in contracts/openapi.yaml as real ASP.NET endpoints matching request/response schemas exactly (not just documented, but functioning), including the /test simulate hook, and remove/replace the placeholder GET / route or keep it out of the OpenAPI doc as now.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: GET /me returns the demo member's profile (name, membership, avatar) with 200 and body matching the Member schema\",\n     \"1: GET /schedule accepts optional array query filters date/type/intensity/timeOfDay and returns matching Session objects with actionState, availabilityLabel, capacityLabel, myBookingId populated correctly\",\n     \"2: GET /sessions/{sessionId} returns a single Session by id with 200\",\n     \"3: GET /sessions/{sessionId} returns 404 not_found when the id does not exist\",\n     \"4: POST /bookings creates a Booking and returns 201 with the created Booking and updated session info\",\n     \"5: POST /bookings returns 409 with one of already_booked, class_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started, cancelled_by_studio, overlap, limit_reached as appropriate, including a refreshed session payload when class_full\",\n     \"6: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo reverses a booking made within the last 5 seconds, returning 200/204 with updated state\",\n     \"7: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo returns 409 undo_expired when called after 5 seconds, and 404 not_found for an unknown bookingId\",\n     \"8: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel cancels a booking, returning a BookingChange indicating whether it was a late cancellation\",\n     \"9: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel returns 409 invalid_booking_state if the booking is not currently Booked, and 404 for unknown id\",\n     \"10: POST /waitlist adds the member to a session's waitlist and returns the Booking with Waitlisted status and position\",\n     \"11: POST /waitlist returns 409 with already_booked, not_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started, or cancelled_by_studio as appropriate\",\n     \"12: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist removes the member from the waitlist and records the booking as Cancelled (not late)\",\n     \"13: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist returns 409 invalid_booking_state if the booking isn't currently Waitlisted, 404 for unknown id\",\n     \"14: GET /me/bookings returns MyBookings split into upcoming and past lists\",\n     \"15: GET /me/stats returns Stats (upcoming count, classes this month, current streak)\",\n     \"16: GET /me/promotion-notices returns unacknowledged PromotionNotices list\",\n     \"17: POST /me/promotion-notices/acknowledge marks all pending notices as acknowledged and returns 204 with empty body\",\n     \"18: POST /test/sessions/{sessionId}/simulate-other-member-cancellation triggers a cancellation by another member on that session, runs waitlist promotion logic, and returns a SimulationResult\",\n     \"19: POST /test/.../simulate-other-member-cancellation returns 404 not_found for unknown sessionId\",\n     \"20: Any endpoint receiving malformed/invalid request bodies or params returns 400 invalid_request\",\n     \"21: Any endpoint that hits a persistence failure returns 500-level storage_failure error code in the standard Error shape\",\n     \"22: Generated OpenAPI document produced by the build matches contracts/openapi.yaml exactly (no extra/missing/altered operations or schemas), verified by the build's conformance check\",\n     \"23: AddOpenApi() remains registered and the generated doc is written to App.Api/openapi so the conformance check can run without touching the database\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Persist all booking-domain data (sessions, bookings, member, promotion notices) in the existing SQLite AppDb via EF Core, with DbSets and seed rows inserted on startup/migration so each list endpoint (schedule, bookings, waitlist, notices) returns at least one row out of the box.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: AppDb gains DbSets for Member, Session, Booking, PromotionNotice (and any join/state needed) backed by SQLite tables\",\n     \"1: A migration or EnsureCreated call creates the schema in app.db (or the configured connection string) on startup/first run\",\n     \"2: Seed data is written so GET /schedule returns at least one session, GET /me/bookings upcoming and past lists are non-empty, GET /me/promotion-notices returns at least one notice, and a full/near-full session exists so waitlist behaviours are exercisable\",\n     \"3: Data created via POST endpoints (bookings, waitlist, cancellations) is persisted to the SQLite file and survives an application restart\",\n     \"4: Reading the same resource twice (e.g. GET /me/bookings after a booking POST) reflects the persisted state, not an in-memory-only change\",\n     \"5: If the database file/connection is unavailable at request time, affected endpoints return the storage_failure error rather than crashing unhandled\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Implement, in the API's business/data layer (not just documented in the contract), the capacity, waitlist, waitlist-promotion, booking/cancellation window, overlap, and limit rules exactly as the contract's responses imply, with a concrete chosen value for limit_reached.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Booking a session at or over capacity is rejected with class_full instead of being created\",\n     \"1: Booking a session under capacity increments booked count and creates a Booked booking\",\n     \"2: Joining the waitlist on a full session creates a Waitlisted booking with the correct position\",\n     \"3: Joining the waitlist on a session that still has free spots is rejected with not_full\",\n     \"4: Cancelling a Booked booking on a full session automatically promotes the first waitlisted member to Booked and creates a promotion notice for them\",\n     \"5: Booking or waitlisting is rejected with outside_booking_window when attempted more than 7 days before the class start or less than 15 minutes before start\",\n     \"6: Booking, cancelling, waitlisting, or leaving-waitlist on a session that has already started is rejected with class_has_started\",\n     \"7: Booking or waitlisting on a studio-cancelled session is rejected with cancelled_by_studio\",\n     \"8: Cancelling a Booked booking less than 2 hours before start is recorded/returned as a late cancellation; 2 hours or more is not late\",\n     \"9: Leaving the waitlist is always recorded as Cancelled with late=false regardless of timing\",\n     \"10: Undoing a booking after 5 seconds from creation is rejected with undo_expired; within 5 seconds it succeeds and reverts the booking/capacity change\",\n     \"11: Booking a session that time-overlaps an existing Booked booking for the same member is rejected with overlap, identifying the conflicting session\",\n     \"12: Booking is rejected with limit_reached once the member already holds a defined maximum number of upcoming Booked sessions (chosen value: 10, matching the product spec since the contract omits the number)\",\n     \"13: Booking a session the member is already booked or waitlisted for is rejected with already_booked\",\n     \"14: The test-only simulate-other-member-cancellation endpoint decrements booked count on the target session and triggers the same waitlist-promotion logic as a real cancellation\",\n     \"15: Promotion notices remain listed via GET /me/promotion-notices until acknowledged via POST /me/promotion-notices/acknowledge, after which they no longer appear\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"sketch\": 2,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Build exactly the 13 operations defined in contracts/openapi.yaml with their exact paths, methods, request/response shapes and status codes; no extra or missing endpoints; no deviation from the contract even where it conflicts with the narrative request.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: GET /me returns the member profile (name, membership, avatar) with 200 and the contract-defined schema\",\n     \"1: GET /schedule accepts array query filters date/type/intensity/timeOfDay and returns a list of Session objects matching the filters\",\n     \"2: GET /schedule with no filters returns all sessions; with filters matching nothing returns an empty list with 200, not an error\",\n     \"3: GET /sessions/{sessionId} returns a single Session with 200, or 404 not_found when the id does not exist\",\n     \"4: POST /bookings creates a booking and returns 201/200 with a Booking on success\",\n     \"5: POST /bookings returns 409 with one of already_booked, class_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started, cancelled_by_studio, overlap, limit_reached, each mapped to the condition that triggers it\",\n     \"6: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo reverts a just-made booking within 5 seconds and returns success; returns undo_expired error after the window or if bookingId doesn't exist (not_found)\",\n     \"7: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel cancels a booking and returns a BookingChange reflecting late-cancellation flag when inside 2 hours of start\",\n     \"8: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel returns invalid_booking_state when the booking is not in a cancellable state, or not_found for unknown bookingId\",\n     \"9: POST /waitlist adds the member to a class waitlist and returns a Booking with Waitlisted status and position\",\n     \"10: POST /waitlist returns 409 for already_booked, not_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started, cancelled_by_studio as appropriate\",\n     \"11: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist removes the member from the waitlist, recording status Cancelled without the late flag\",\n     \"12: POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist returns not_found/invalid_booking_state for a bookingId that is not an active waitlist entry\",\n     \"13: GET /me/bookings returns MyBookings with upcoming (booked+waitlisted) and past (attended+cancelled) lists\",\n     \"14: GET /me/stats returns Stats (upcoming count, classes this month, streak) matching current booking data\",\n     \"15: GET /me/promotion-notices returns PromotionNotices listing unacknowledged waitlist-promotion notices\",\n     \"16: POST /me/promotion-notices/acknowledge marks all current notices as acknowledged and returns 204 with no body\",\n     \"17: POST /test/sessions/{sessionId}/simulate-other-member-cancellation cancels another member's booking on that session, triggers waitlist promotion, and returns a SimulationResult\",\n     \"18: Any request to an undefined route or wrong method returns a standard 404/405, not a custom shape\",\n     \"19: All error responses use only the fixed Error code enum values; unrecognised internal failures map to storage_failure or invalid_request rather than leaking raw exceptions\",\n     \"20: class_full errors include a refreshed session object in the response body 