sen\": \"All booking-related business rules are enforced server-side in the data/business layer behind the API, independent of any UI, covering the specific numeric windows and limits given in the contract (7 days / 15 minutes / 2 hours / 5 seconds / 10 bookings).\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Booking a session is rejected with class_full once bookedCount reaches capacity; capacity is never exceeded by a successful booking\",\n     \"1: When a session is full, joinWaitlist succeeds and assigns the next sequential waitlist position\",\n     \"2: joinWaitlist is rejected with not_full when the session still has open spots\",\n     \"3: createBooking is rejected with outside_booking_window when requested more than 7 days before start or within 15 minutes of start\",\n     \"4: createBooking/joinWaitlist is rejected with class_has_started once the session's start time has passed\",\n     \"5: createBooking/joinWaitlist is rejected with cancelled_by_studio when the session status is Cancelled by studio\",\n     \"6: createBooking is rejected with overlap when the member already holds a Booked session whose time range intersects the requested session, and the error identifies the conflicting class\",\n     \"7: createBooking is rejected with limit_reached once the member already holds 10 upcoming Booked sessions; a concrete limit value of 10 is enforced in code even though the contract names the error without a number\",\n     \"8: createBooking is rejected with already_booked if the member already holds a Booked or Waitlisted entry for that same session\",\n     \"9: undoBooking succeeds only when called within 5 seconds of the original booking's creation timestamp; later calls return undo_expired\",\n     \"10: cancelBooking sets a 'late' flag on the resulting BookingChange when cancellation occurs less than 2 hours before the session start, and leaves it unset otherwise\",\n     \"11: leaveWaitlist records the entry as Cancelled without ever setting the late flag, regardless of timing\",\n     \"12: When a Booked member cancels a full class, the first Waitlisted member for that session is automatically promoted to Booked status and a promotion notice record is created for them\",\n     \"13: The test-only simulateOtherMemberCancellation endpoint cancels another member's booking and triggers the same promotion logic, returning the promotion outcome\",\n     \"14: Promotion notices remain listed via GET /me/promotion-notices until explicitly acknowledged via POST /me/promotion-notices/acknowledge, after which they no longer appear in subsequent GETs\",\n     \"15: All these rule checks happen in the API/service layer so that calling the endpoints directly (bypassing any UI) still enforces every rule\",\n     \"16: Automated tests exist covering: capacity-full rejection, waitlist join success, waitlist promotion, booking-window edges, late-cancellation flag, overlap rejection, 10-booking limit, and rejection of booking past/cancelled classes\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"sketch\": 3,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Implement all 13 operations defined in contracts/openapi.yaml with exact paths, methods, request/response schemas, status codes, and error codes, as server endpoints in the existing .NET API project; no UI screens are built here.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: GET /api/me returns the demo member record (name, membership, avatar) with 200 and a body matching the Member schema.\",\n     \"1: GET /api/schedule accepts repeated/array query params date, type, intensity, timeOfDay and returns 200 with an array of Session objects matching the filters.\",\n     \"2: GET /api/schedule with no filters returns all sessions for the default/current period.\",\n     \"3: Each returned Session includes computed fields actionState, availabilityLabel, capacityLabel, and myBookingId (null if the requesting member has no booking on that session).\",\n     \"4: GET /api/sessions/{sessionId} returns 200 with a single Session object for a valid id.\",\n     \"5: GET /api/sessions/{sessionId} returns 404 not_found when the sessionId does not exist.\",\n     \"6: POST /api/bookings with a valid sessionId creates a Booked record and returns 201 with the Booking object.\",\n     \"7: POST /api/bookings returns 409 with one of already_booked, class_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started, cancelled_by_studio, overlap, limit_reached, each with the matching Error.code.\",\n     \"8: 409 class_full error response includes a refreshed Session object in the error's session field reflecting current capacity/waitlist state.\",\n     \"9: POST /api/bookings/{bookingId}/undo within 5 seconds of booking reverts the booking (removes it / restores prior state) and returns 200 with a BookingChange.\",\n     \"10: POST /api/bookings/{bookingId}/undo after 5 seconds returns 409 undo_expired.\",\n     \"11: POST /api/bookings/{bookingId}/undo on a non-existent or non-undoable booking returns 404 not_found or 409 invalid_booking_state as appropriate.\",\n     \"12: POST /api/bookings/{bookingId}/cancel on a Booked booking marks it Cancelled and returns 200 with a BookingChange.\",\n     \"13: POST /api/bookings/{bookingId}/cancel sets a late-cancellation flag on the response when executed less than 2 hours before the session start.\",\n     \"14: POST /api/bookings/{bookingId}/cancel on an already-cancelled, attended, or missing booking returns 409 invalid_booking_state or 404 not_found.\",\n     \"15: POST /api/waitlist with a full session's sessionId creates a Waitlisted booking with a waitlist position and returns 201.\",\n     \"16: POST /api/waitlist returns 409 with one of already_booked, not_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started, cancelled_by_studio.\",\n     \"17: POST /api/bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist on a Waitlisted booking sets status Cancelled (not late) and returns 200 with a BookingChange.\",\n     \"18: POST /api/bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist on a non-waitlisted or missing booking returns 409 invalid_booking_state or 404 not_found.\",\n     \"19: GET /api/me/bookings returns 200 with a MyBookings object listing upcoming (Booked/Waitlisted) and past (Cancelled/Attended) bookings.\",\n     \"20: GET /api/me/stats returns 200 with a Stats object (upcoming count, classes-this-month count, current streak).\",\n     \"21: GET /api/me/promotion-notices returns 200 with a PromotionNotices object listing unacknowledged waitlist-promotion notices.\",\n     \"22: POST /api/me/promotion-notices/acknowledge marks all outstanding promotion notices as acknowledged and returns 204 with no body.\",\n     \"23: POST /api/test/sessions/{sessionId}/simulate-other-member-cancellation cancels a booked seat on the given session, triggers waitlist promotion, and returns 200 with a SimulationResult.\",\n     \"24: simulate-other-member-cancellation on a session with no bookings or an invalid sessionId returns 404 not_found or 409 invalid_request.\",\n     \"25: Any request with malformed/missing required fields returns 400 invalid_request.\",\n     \"26: Any unexpected persistence failure returns 500 storage_failure rather than leaking a stack trace.\",\n     \"27: The generated OpenAPI document produced by the running app (AddOpenApi) matches contracts/openapi.yaml byte-for-byte/structurally, verified by the build's conformance check.\",\n     \"28: The server is mounted under base path /api as declared by the contract's server URL.\",\n     \"29: The existing GET / route continues to return 200 'API is up' and stays excluded from the generated OpenAPI document.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Persist all booking-app data (sessions, bookings, member, promotion notices) in the project's SQLite database via EF Core, with the database created/migrated and a small seed dataset inserted so every list endpoint returns at least one row.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: AppDb gains DbSets for Member, Session, Booking, PromotionNotice (or equivalent) with EF Core entity configuration mapping to SQLite tables.\",\n     \"1: On startup or via migration, the SQLite database file (app.db by default, or the 'App' connection string) is created with these tables if not already present.\",\n     \"2: Seed data is written containing: 1 demo member (Alex Rivera, Unlimited Monthly, 'AR'), multiple class sessions spanning the supported types, at least one full class, at least one almost-full class, at least one studio-cancelled class, and a handful of bookings for the demo member (upcoming, waitlisted, and past/attended) so that GET /schedule, GET /me/bookings, GET /me/stats, and GET /me/promotion-notices each return non-empty results.\",\n     \"3: GET /me/bookings after a fresh seed returns at least one upcoming and one past booking without requiring any prior write via the API.\",\n     \"4: GET /schedule after a fresh seed returns a non-empty list including at least one full and one cancelled-by-studio session.\",\n     \"5: Bookings created, undone, cancelled, or promoted through the API are persisted in SQLite and survive a process restart (read back correctly on next GET).\",\n     \"6: If the SQLite file/connection is unavailable or a write fails, the affected endpoint returns 500 storage_failure instead of crashing or returning partial data.\",\n     \"7: No migration/seed step requires or exposes any destructive operation (e.g. dropping existing data) when run against a database that already has rows.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All business rules listed (capacity, waitlist incl. promotion, booking window, cancellation window/late flag, overlap, booking limit) are enforced server-side in the API/business layer for every relevant operation, not just documented in the contract.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Booking a session at or beyond its capacity is rejected with 409 class_full (capacity rule enforced regardless of what the client sends).\",\n     \"1: Joining the waitlist on a full session succeeds and assigns the next sequential waitlist position.\",\n     \"2: Joining the waitlist on a non-full session is rejected with 409 not_full.\",\n     \"3: When a Booked member cancels (via cancel endpoint or the simulate-other-member-cancellation test hook), the first member in waitlist order for that session is automatically promoted to Booked, their waitlist entry is removed, and a promotion notice record is created for them.\",\n     \"4: Promotion notices are returned by GET /me/promotion-notices until the member calls POST /me/promotion-notices/acknowledge, after which they no longer appear in subsequent GET calls.\",\n     \"5: Booking or waitlisting a session more than 7 days before its start time is rejected with 409 outside_booking_window.\",\n     \"6: Booking or waitlisting a session less than 15 minutes before its start time is rejected with 409 outside_booking_window, and once the session has started it is rejected with 409 class_has_started instead.\",\n     \"7: Cancelling a booking 2 or more hours before the session start succeeds with no late flag set.\",\n     \"8: Cancelling a booking less than 2 hours before the session start succeeds but the response/BookingChange marks it as a late cancellation.\",\n     \"9: Leaving a waitlist is always recorded as a plain Cancelled status, never flagged as a late cancellation, regardless of timing.\",\n     \"10: Attempting to book, cancel, or waitlist a session whose status is Cancelled by studio is rejected with 409 cancelled_by_studio.\",\n     \"11: Attempting to create a booking that time-overlaps with another of the member's existing Booked sessions is rejected with 409 overlap, and the error payload names/identifies the conflicting session.\",\n     \"12: Attempting to create an 11th simultaneous upcoming Booked booking for the member is rejected with 409 limit_reached (limit fixed at 10, chosen since the contract names the error but omits the number).\",\n     \"13: Attempting to book, cancel, waitlist, undo, or leave-waitlist on a session that has already started is rejected with 409 class_has_started / invalid_booking_state rather than silently succeeding.\",\n     \"14: All of the above checks run inside the request-handling/business logic layer against current database state, not merely reflected in UI button disabling (none exists here since this is API-only).\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nList the disagreements."}